From adffa7eaef4e52bbc52fcd99d6e887927f38889e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:02:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 43/59] fix(dolt): report external (unmanaged) server in dolt
 status/dump diagnostics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After the local->external Dolt migration the town connects to a launchd-managed
sql-server on 127.0.0.1:<port> that gt does not own. IsRunning correctly reports
it reachable but with PID 0 — a deliberate safety return so `gt dolt stop`
cannot kill the shared server. `gt dolt status`/`dump` then presented the
gt-managed defaults as if they were the live server's: PID 0, the empty
<townRoot>/.dolt-data shim as the data dir, and a tail of the frozen dead-daemon
daemon/dolt.log. Read together that looks like "PID 0 / data missing / logs
frozen months ago", so the deacon/boot health check escalated CRITICAL "Dolt
server unreachable" against a fully healthy server, in a loop
(hq-80nx/hq-89vh/hq-ysvn).

When a server is reachable on the town port but not gt-managed (PID 0), resolve
the real listening process (read-only: lsof/ss for the PID, its --data-dir and
--config from the process args) and present those instead:
- status: "reachable (external, PID <real> — not gt-managed)" + live data dir
- dump: real PID + real data dir + external note; skip tailing the stale
  gt-managed log rather than presenting it as the live server's.

IsRunning is left unchanged: it must keep returning PID 0 for an unmanaged
server so no stop/kill path targets the foreign PID (the hq-rhlx footgun of
killing the shared launchd Dolt). The new read-only InspectExternalServer helper
never feeds a kill path.

Sibling to 8752fc20 (ListDatabases loopback fix), same root family: gate on
reachability/ownership, not the loopback host-heuristic or gt-managed PID.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
